  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Ma tribe intel on the Meng Qiu heroes assembly names him as the fighter Nu Er tribe has sent, and treats that move as strong enough to threaten Lui tribe.",
      "chapters": [
        489
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_ma_tribe",
        "fac_nu_er_tribe"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Later Ge tribe reports to Fang Yuan under the Chang Shan Yin name repeat that Nu Er tribe’s representative at Meng Qiu is a rank five Gu Master named Nu Er Tu.",
      "chapters": [
        496
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_ge_tribe",
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "char_chang_shan_yin",
        "sys_gu_master"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "At Meng Qiu his leopard group fights Jiang Bao Ya’s rats. He stands with mutated leopards beside him, mocks Jiang Bao Ya’s six hundred and fifty thousand rats as oversized, and calls for that fight to spread his name across Northern Plains. When Jiang Bao Ya answers with Rat Epidemic, Nu Er Tu answers with the killer move Leopard Dash, which more than doubles the leopards’ battle strength and raises their speed about eightfold so they break out of the poison gas and overrun the field.",
      "chapters": [
        523
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "five-beast-kings",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_jiang_bao_ya",
        "reg_northern_plains",
        "move_rat_epidemic",
        "move_leopard_dash"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He was not originally an enslavement path Gu Master and switched into it midway, yet that win over a veteran enslavement master raises him into the northern plains enslavement master ranks beside Jiang Bao Ya, Yang Po Ying, Ma Zun, and Chang Shan Yin as five beast kings.",
      "chapters": [
        525
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "five-beast-kings",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_yang_po_ying",
        "char_ma_zun"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Later talk names him Leopard King Nu Er Tu with a glimpse leopard group among those five, and recalls that only five enslavement path masters appeared across the whole Imperial Court contest.",
      "chapters": [
        527
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "five-beast-kings",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "evt_arc_imperial_court_contest"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Battle reports next say his army rests and captures wild leopard groups instead of resuming the march, and Ma Ying Jie notes that he does this without asking help from the Gu Immortal behind him.",
      "chapters": [
        529
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "five-beast-kings",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_ma_ying_jie",
        "sys_gu_immortal"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He later takes Tao tribe’s submission after pressing that alliance, then loses to Yang tribe when leopards cannot match the combined eagle and rat groups.",
      "chapters": [
        536
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "five-beast-kings",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_tao_tribe",
        "fac_yang_tribe"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "More than a year after advancing to rank six with Nu Er tribe’s help, he still browses treasure yellow heaven as a new Gu Immortal. The same stretch names him great-grandson of Gu Immortal Nu Er Chi, recalls his Imperial Court contest role among the five beast kings, and shows him questioning Shi Zhong’s wealth mortal Gu before backing out of the buy when another divine sense rushes the stock.",
      "chapters": [
        2262
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "gu-immortal-years",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_treasure_yellow_heaven",
        "char_shi_zhong",
        "sys_mortal_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The fan translation writes Nu Er Tu and Leopard King Nu Er Tu. No Chinese characters for the personal name appear in the English chapter text used here.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "translation-notes",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    }
  ],
